      "standardized_narrative": "During 2024 the syndicate recorded gross prior-year reserve strengthening of $58.972m (c.6.54% of opening gross claims outstanding) driven by adverse claims development across several classes, particularly Non-Marine Liability (US casualty) and Marine & Energy Liability. The deterioration followed completion of reserving reviews, observed large single claimant settlements and litigation financing trends in the US, and adverse development in Aviation, Marine Hull and Offshore Energy. The syndicate also increased IBNR allowances related to the Russia/Ukraine conflict (expected net cost $4.5m).",
